    "body": "In a rough attempt to repeat Joule's famous experiment you begin with 0.6 kg of a liquid at room temperature in a not very well insulated container. You stir the liquid until a thermometer shows that its temperature increased by 0.3 K. In the process you did 7000 J of work on the liquid by stirring it.\n\nWhat is the magnitude of the thermal energy transfer, $|Q|$, from the liquid to its surroundings due to a temperature difderence that occurred while you stirred? Note: the specific heat capacity of liquid is 4200 J/kg/K.",
